From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:04:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(claude-native): show a parent agent's follow-ups in the
 sub-agent chat

When a Claude parent messages a running sub-agent (SendMessage to a
background agent or teammate), Claude records the message in the child's
transcript as hidden context: isMeta with origin {"kind": "coordinator"}
and the text "The coordinator sent a message while you were working: ...".
The bridge dropped every hidden record that was not a completion, so the
child's chat in the web UI showed the child replying to a prompt nobody
could see.

Keep coordinator-origin records as hidden (is_meta) messages and render
them in the child's chat as a muted "Message from parent agent" system
marker, the same treatment a background-task wake already gets. Messages
in the parent chat stay hidden, and a human typing the same text still
gets an ordinary bubble.

Not upstream yet: proposed from fix/claude-native-coordinator-messages; drop this copy once it merges.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
